;; expect: main.grow refused realize_descent
;; §8.4 slice 3.28 rule 4 (landing 3; T3's canonical refusal): a template calling itself at a type
;; built from its own type parameter — f[A] recursing at f[List A] — is refused at its declaration,
;; where the self-call's type arguments are read: the shape set would grow without bound. A
;; refusal before any instance is built, which is what the budget and this check are — totality
;; is not compiler termination (law §12.5, T3's risk column).
(import Init Nat.sub)
(fn idl ((a Type) (xs (List a))) (List a) xs)
(fn grow ((a Type) (f (-> a a)) (x a) (n Nat)) Nat (measure n)
  (if (= n 0) 0 (grow idl (List.cons x List.nil) (- n 1))))
